[Zhelobenko, <<cite:zh:cg>>] Let $L(\lambda)$ be the simple finite dimensional module over $\mathfrak{gl}(n)$ of highest weight $\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{n})$, with basis as described in Theorem <<ref:Theorem: GT theorem>>. The action of the generators $c_{rs}$ of $\Gamma$ (see (<<ref:Equation: c_mk>>)) is given by

\begin{equation}
c_{rs}(T(v))=\gamma_{rs}(v)T(v),
\end{equation}

where $\gamma_{rs}(v)$ are the symmetric polynomials defined in (<<ref:Equation: gamma mk>>).
